# Cloudflare `_headers` — parsed by the Worker's static-asset layer, never served
# (a request for /_headers is a 404, verified).
#
# Every rule here was written against a MEASURED difference between what Vercel
# sent and what Cloudflare sends by default. None of it is decorative, and the
# first block is the one that matters: nothing in the test suite can see it.

# Vercel set all three of these implicitly on every response. Cloudflare sets none.
#
#   Access-Control-Allow-Origin — the JSON Schemas are published under their
#     canonical $id URLs (https://archlang.uk/plan.schema.json is what
#     src/plan-json.ts writes into every Plan JSON document), and llms.txt
#     advertises the whole root as machine-fetchable. Dropping CORS silently
#     breaks any browser-context validator or agent. NO TEST IN THIS REPO WOULD
#     CATCH IT: scripts/smoke.mjs is Node fetch and Playwright's `request`
#     fixture are both exempt from CORS.
#   Content-Disposition — without it a `text/markdown` response is offered as a
#     download instead of shown, which defeats the append-`.md` convention.
#   Strict-Transport-Security — browsers hold Vercel's two-year max-age today.
#     Matching it keeps the header refreshing instead of silently expiring in
#     2028. `includeSubDomains` is deliberately ABSENT, as it was on Vercel:
#     turning it on would newly bind every subdomain of archlang.uk.
/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Content-Disposition: inline
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000

# Cloudflare's default for every asset is `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` —
# correct, but it revalidates every hashed bundle on every page load, where Vercel
# marked fingerprinted files immutable. Vite/VitePress fingerprint everything under
# /assets/, so those URLs can never change identity: cache them for a year. Every
# other route keeps the revalidating default, which is what makes a deploy visible
# immediately.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The raw markdown copies (`/<page>.md`, the append-`.md` convention llms.txt
# advertises). Cloudflare types these `text/markdown` with NO charset, where Vercel
# sent `text/markdown; charset=utf-8`. A `text/*` response with no charset is
# latin-1 by default in some clients, which mojibakes every em-dash on these pages.
# One rule per route, NOT a `/*.md` glob: a glob also matched a missing `/x.md`, whose
# 404 HTML page then went out labelled `text/markdown`. The routes come from the PAGES
# and SITE_PAGES tables in sync-docs.mjs, so a new page is covered by `gen:docs-headers`.
# BEGIN GENERATED by `npm run gen:docs-headers` — do not edit; edit the tables in docs-site/sync-docs.mjs

/reference.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8

/showcase.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8

